From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Nova: Class-AB headphones and RX compander initialization

Use Class-AB LOHIFI for the Nova's remaining headphone distortion and
initialize both RX companders explicitly off at boot.
The device-specific settings live in UCM quirks selected by the root DT
model, since the Nova shares its AYN-Odin2 sound card identity.

The LOHIFI default and removal of RX compander enable writes are already
provided by alsa-ucm-conf 1.2.16.1. Keep the mode write in its upstream
position before RX routing is enabled.

Reference: https://github.com/ROCKNIX/distribution/pull/3481
---
--- a/ucm2/codecs/wcd938x/HeadphoneEnableSeq.conf
+++ b/ucm2/codecs/wcd938x/HeadphoneEnableSeq.conf
@@ -1,3 +1,6 @@
+Define.WcdHphMode "CLS_H_LOHIFI"
+Include.nova.File "/Retroid/Nova/HeadphoneMode.conf"
+
 EnableSequence [
 	cset "name='HPHL_RDAC Switch' 1"
 	cset "name='HPHR_RDAC Switch' 1"
@@ -7,5 +10,5 @@
 	cset "name='HPHL_COMP Switch' 0"
 	cset "name='CLSH Switch' 1"
 	cset "name='LO Switch' 1"
-	cset "name='RX HPH Mode' CLS_H_LOHIFI"
+	cset "name='RX HPH Mode' ${var:WcdHphMode}"
 ]
--- a/ucm2/AYN/Odin2/AYN-Odin2.conf
+++ b/ucm2/AYN/Odin2/AYN-Odin2.conf
@@ -29,3 +29,4 @@
 Include.card-init.File "/lib/card-init.conf"
 Include.ctl-remap.File "/lib/ctl-remap.conf"
 Include.wcd-init.File "/codecs/wcd938x/init.conf"
+Include.nova-init.File "/Retroid/Nova/init.conf"
